IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order (O 1, 2004 Revised Edition, 29.2.2004; G.N. No. S 307/96), made under s 60 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-order-1996/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-OR1.20040229.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited): the Order BEFORE S 600/2014 (15 September 2014) amended paragraph 1(f) and deleted paragraph 2.
-- The text after S 600/2014 is `sgba-i-exempt-1996.l4` (lawplain). Only paragraphs 1(f) and 2, which S 600/2014 changed, are encoded here; paragraphs 1(a) to (e) and (g) read the same in both.

§ `Paragraphs 1(f) and 2 as the Revised Edition 2004 prints them`

-- src:32 | (f) computer on-line services other than computer on-line
-- src:33 | services subject to a class licence under the Broadcasting
-- src:34 | (Class Licence) Notification (N 1); or
@ref O 1 para 1(f) (RevEd 2004): computer on-line services other than those subject to a class licence under N 1 (src:32-34)
GIVEN `it is a computer on-line service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subject to a class licence under the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (N 1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`O 1 para 1(f) the service is exempt from sections 8 and 9 (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `it is a computer on-line service` AND (NOT `it is subject to a class licence under the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (N 1)`)

-- src:39 | 2. The exemption under paragraph 1 (f) includes computer on-line
-- src:40 | services provided, other than for business, political or religious
-- src:44 | purposes, by individual Internet Content Providers as defined in the
-- src:45 | Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (N 1).
@ref O 1 para 2 (RevEd 2004): the exemption under paragraph 1(f) includes computer on-line services provided, other than for business, political or religious purposes, by individual Internet Content Providers (src:39-45)
GIVEN `it is a computer on-line service provided by an individual Internet Content Provider as defined in N 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided for business, political or religious purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`O 1 para 2 the exemption under paragraph 1(f) includes the service (RevEd 2004)` MEANS
    `it is a computer on-line service provided by an individual Internet Content Provider as defined in N 1` AND (NOT `it is provided for business, political or religious purposes`)
